Template: the frontend-design skill ships this template as a reference implementation. Read its SKILL.md first, then read templates/web-resume.html and templates/web-resume.info.md as described in the case-template section, and treat them as the baseline for layout skeleton, color roles, type hierarchy, and interaction.

Content to replace:
- The name, role, intro, and contact entries in person become your real details; keep the name to two to four characters and fill all four contact entries;
- summary is one concrete paragraph about what you shipped and what reusable artefact you left behind, not a list of adjectives;
- Keep three roles in jobs with two to three result lines each, and lead with numbers instead of responsibilities;
- Keep three items in projects (a three-column grid), about five in skills (percent is relative on one scale), and four in education;
- Update the language, title, and description in meta.

Design goal:
Keep the visual language of the template: a paper ground, an oversized serif name, a letterspaced role line, the ruled entry grid with a left date column, hairline skill bars, and the two-column education block. Adjust hue and type within that language, but do not turn it into a card flow, and do not add a portrait photo, rounded cards, or gradients.

